# Code owners for this repository.
#
# `@catincloudlabs` is a USER account, not the `catincloud-labs` organization
# that owns this repository. CODEOWNERS resolves users and teams; an
# organization name on its own is not a valid owner, and this organization has
# no teams, so a `@catincloud-labs/<team>` entry would resolve to nothing
# silently.
#
# An entry here is inert unless the account it names has write access to this
# repository. When it does not, the entry is reported as "Unknown owner" rather
# than failing loudly, and `GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/codeowners/errors` is what
# says so. That error does not distinguish a misspelled name from a real account
# that is simply missing the grant, so check both.
#
# Two owners on one pattern means a review from EITHER satisfies the
# code-owner requirement. GitHub forbids approving your own pull request, so
# a single-owner file leaves the requirement unsatisfiable for that owner --
# they can only bypass it. The second entry is what makes the requirement
# satisfiable in both directions, and it is deliberate, not a courtesy.

